From: Alessio Bogani <alessio.bogani@elettra.eu>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: Makefile.xpl: fix SPL alignment with GNU dd

GNU dd requires cbs= when conv=block is used, so the SPL alignment
command fails before producing the aligned image.  conv=block is not
needed here: conv=sync already pads the final short input block to the
requested four-byte boundary.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Alessio Bogani <alessio.bogani@elettra.eu>
---
 scripts/Makefile.xpl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/Makefile.xpl b/scripts/Makefile.xpl
index c39c2a9319..8d5b6de5b0 100644
--- a/scripts/Makefile.xpl
+++ b/scripts/Makefile.xpl
@@ -254,6 +254,6 @@ endif
 
 $(obj)/$(SPL_BIN)-align.bin: $(obj)/$(SPL_BIN).bin
-	@dd if=$< of=$@ conv=block,sync bs=4 2>/dev/null;
+	@dd if=$< of=$@ conv=sync bs=4 2>/dev/null;
 
 spl/boot.bin: $(obj)/$(SPL_BIN)-align.bin FORCE
 	$(call if_changed,mkimage)
